sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg critical wavenumber calibrated to 1.754 µm at 19 Ma (Pearson r = 0.999998, RMSE = 0.000250 on nine modes). The equal-diffusion control is now the real part of the complex eigenvalue: measured envelope -0.4051 versus analytical -0.4099. A six-point D_v sweep lengthens lambda_sigma monotonically from 1.960 µm to 2.614 µm. The early 2D field locks to lambda_sigma = 2.253 µm. Detail wavelengths at fixed mode number N = 55.87 are 2.040 µm (succini, 44 Ma), 1.754 µm (berryi, 19 Ma) and 1.718 µm (affinis, 0 Ma). The gallery plate remains an amber spiral, not a 1.8 µm micrograph. Overall 88.1/100 (faithfulness 87.6, reproducibility 89.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_berryi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 420283 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 7dc94265a3154b3e4b9205958a17c4842cf11af7642327c6a660f3a6c7f80a99 (sha256 7dc94265a3154b3e4b9205958a17c4842cf11af7642327c6a660f3a6c7f80a99), spec_fingerprint fe2e74bbe1194adf9f66d7de47fdd4b5119a2272757767687404f3140401fa54. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fe2e74bbe1194adf9f66d7de47fdd4b5119a2272757767687404f3140401fa54; artifact_sha256: 7dc94265a3154b3e4b9205958a17c4842cf11af7642327c6a660f3a6c7f80a99. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber condition. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Grimaldi 1987 Hispaniolan amber Drosophilidae; Grimaldi 1995 on Dominican amber age.; reconstructed_in_script: Parameters a=0.2305, b=0.7942, D_u=0.03686, D_v=1.721 with the unit set so lambda_c = 1.754 µm. | Chronoseries 2.040 → 1.754 → 1.718 µm at fixed mode number 98/1.754. | Complex-mode envelope for the equal-diffusion control and a six-point D_v sweep of lambda_sigma.; transfer_boundary: Ages and tissue wavelengths are Project Delphi chronoseries assignments, not quotations from Grimaldi 1987. | Murray 1981 scale argument is transferred from coat markings to the amber chronospecies metric.; does_not_claim: That a fossil micrograph at 1.754 µm was fitted pixel-for-pixel. | That the GIF terminal frame is a raw PDE field; it is the gallery plate after the growth sequence. | That raising D_v is how succini differs from berryi. The chronospecies change is the metric, and the D_v sweep is a separate expressivity test.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Closed in Pass 2. Equal-diffusion envelope is -0.4051 versus analytical Re(sigma) -0.4099.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Closed in Pass 2. Early 2D FFT peak equals lambda_sigma (2.253 µm) and the D_v sweep is monotone.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Open. No second assessor. The gallery plate is not a 1.8 µm fossil micrograph; specimen-match is not raised to the GIF crop score.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.881"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

